Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:27:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] autokernel serving: every task of OUR pinned server
 inside cpu_list before measuring (re-pin + refuse + post-run re-check)

Finding (workspace-58, 2026-10-22): a `taskset -c 184-191` HIP llama-server
had ONE early ROCr thread on 0-191; installed ROCr 6.2 os::CreateThread hands
pthread_create an all-CPU affinity unless HSA_OVERRIDE_CPU_AFFINITY_DEBUG=0.

loop/launch_affinity.py (twin of epyc-orchestrator scripts/server/
launch_affinity.py): task_masks, escapes, pin_all_tasks (sub-masks kept,
repeat until clean), pin_own_child (acts only on a direct child -- prove OUR
pid).

serving._measure_once: after health and before any request, a pinned recipe
runs pin_own_child; a remaining escape raises ServerDied. The result is
recorded as residency.affinity, and affinity.escapes_end re-reads the masks
after the measurement round (read-only).

Deliberately NOT here: the ROCr env knob (layer 1). The loader env is
identity-bearing across resolved_recipe, unified_planner,
production_enrollment, runtime_identity and legacy_targets; a first attempt
that added it as a loader-owned key failed ~173 AK tests on env-equality
identity checks. Adding it is an AutoKernel identity decision (package D2,
root artifacts/operator/stack-change-gpu-thread-pin-20261022/PACKAGE.md).

Tests: test_launch_affinity.py (new) + the 16 AK files the first attempt
broke + recipe/hip/gpu-profile/cpu-serving files: 312 passed, 2 failed --
both test_serial_roster.py::test_shared_author_sandbox_* and both fail
identically on origin/main (pre-existing).

